STEP 1 — DELTA
- [NEW] ds-apip.threema.ch (directory server, 203.56.112.214 = SAME IP as in-scope apip.threema.ch). Source: `threema-desktop` `config.rs::Config::production()`; API surface enumerated from in-scope source.
- [NEW] ds-apip-work.threema.ch (legacy work directory server, 203.56.112.209 = SAME IP as in-scope work.threema.ch); GET / → 401.
- [NEW] ds-blobp-upload.threema.ch (blob upload, 203.56.112.217); GET /upload → 403. Download shards ds-blobp-{x} do NOT resolve publicly.
- [NEW] avatar.threema.ch (gateway avatar server, 203.56.112.237); GET / and /ECHOECHO → 403.
- [NEW] blob-mirror-{0..f}.threema.ch resolves (multi-device blob mirror; 203.56.112.247/114.247 pools).
- [CHANGED] Chat server pattern is actually `ds.g-{hex}.0.threema.ch` (ports 5222/443), NOT `g-*.0.threema.ch`; sampled 0,1,a,f → NO public DNS. Chat surface is bootstrap-gated.
- [CHANGED] safe-*.threema.ch template confirmed as `safe-{backupIdPrefix8}.threema.ch` but sampled prefixes 0-6,9,a,f → NO public DNS. Backup surface hidden.
- [CHANGED] apip.threema.ch reclassified: alias of ds-apip.threema.ch; validated unauthenticated GET responses (below).
- [NEW] Directory API spec published in-scope (`directory.openapi.yml`): /identity/{blob_cred,revoke,set_revocation_key,check_revocation_key,ws/revoke,sfu_cred,update_work_info} + work /fetch2,/identities,/directory + /api-client/v1/{user-properties,remote-secret}; challenge-response auth (BLAKE2b/X25519HSalsa20, salts 'dir'/'wdir', personal '3ma-csp'); /fetch2,/identities,/directory and /api-client/* resolve to ds-apip-work.
- [NEW] Validated passive responses: GET /identity/fetch_bulk → 200 `{"identities":[]}`; /identity/create → 200 `{"success":false,"error":"Invalid public key"}`; /identity/{blob_cred,sfu_cred,check_revocation_key} → 200 `{"success":false,"error":"Identity not found"}`.
- [NEW] web.threema.ch → 301 to web.threema.com (off-scope third-party); work.threema.ch → 301 /en/login; shop.threema.ch → 301 /en.
- [SCOPE NOTE] ds-*, avatar, blob-mirror, sfu are not on the program's enumerated target list; they share origin IPs with in-scope apip/work — confirm scope before testing them beyond passive.

